# The seeds of the compiler: released executables of the source in compiler/ for
# x86-64 Linux, one a line, the last line the one the build is pinned to.
#
#   version revision sha256 url
#
# version   number of the seed; the release is tagged seed-<version> and
#           the file is named ailc-<version>
# revision  the commit whose source in compiler/ it was
#           built from (in the directory stage1/ up to seed 2); built
#           again from that source by itself it gives the same file
# sha256    of the file; a copy with another checksum is refused
# url       where the release keeps it
#
# A local copy is seed/ailc-<version>, which git ignores. Earlier lines
# stay, so that an older revision can still be built with its own seed.
#
# From seed 7 on a seed has in it the image of the runtime that a C
# compiler built at its revision, and another C compiler may write other
# bytes. The release keeps that image beside the seed as rt-<version>:
# make RT=<that file> at the revision gives the seed again.
